{"kind":"stack","id":"s-living-groups","title":"Grouping living things","theme":{"background":"#f4fbf2","foreground":"#1d3b1f","font":"Trebuchet MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Living things"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Things that grow, need food and water, breathe and can reproduce."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Grouping"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Sorting things into sets that share features, such as animals with backbones or plants that flower."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"fish"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which group is a fish in?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a1","label":"Animals with backbones","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a2","label":"Animals without legs","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a3","label":"Animals that live in trees","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which plant is in the group of plants that flower?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a1","label":"Rose","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a2","label":"Moss","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a3","label":"Fern","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Which feature would you use to group a cat and a dog together?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a1","label":"Both have fur and give birth to live young","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a2","label":"Both live in water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a3","label":"Both have leaves","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Aoife finds a bug, a bird and a snail. Which should she group first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Group by whether they have wings","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Group by whether they can move","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Aoife puts the bug and bird together. The snail sits alone. Good sorting!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Aoife finds all three can move, but in different ways. She tries again with more features."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which is a useful reason to group living things?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a1","label":"It helps us find and compare living things","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a2","label":"It makes living things stop changing","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a3","label":"It means every group has only one member","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which group does a whale belong to?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a1","label":"Animals with backbones that breathe air","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a2","label":"Animals with backbones that breathe water through gills","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a3","label":"Animals without backbones","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-t","content":"You finished the grouping living things lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. Sorting living things by shared features helps scientists understand all the different kinds of life around us."}],"actions":[]}}
